      <h1 class="mt-4 text-[clamp(2.75rem,5vw+1rem,5rem)] leading-[0.98]">A butcher's shop full of flowers</h1>
      <p class="body-copy mt-7 text-[1.125rem]">Roz grew up on the Slopes among her grandmother's dahlias and spent eight years building weddings for an event studio in Philadelphia. In 2020 she came home with Teo, a line cook who liked getting up early, and found a corner butcher's shop from 1905 for rent at the foot of Mercer Steps.</p>
      <p class="body-copy mt-5 text-[1.125rem]">The white tiles and the marble counter stayed. The old meat locker became the flower cooler, and its back room, the locker room, seats twelve for the workshops. From April to October the pails stand on the sidewalk; in winter they move into the window.</p>
